# Labels and status

**Site settings > Connectors & Apps** lists each app, API token and connector as one connection.
Open a connection to see what it sent.

## Labels

Every record carries a label that the sending app chose. One app can use more than one label. For
example, an app can label its glucose readings with the name of the sensor and label everything
else with its own name. Nocturne lists each label inside the connection that sent the records.
The label is also the name that you see when you delete the data of one stream.

Records that no connection is known to have sent are listed under **Other sources**.

## Status

Nocturne counts the records that a connection sent in the last 30 days. A connection that sent
nothing in that time shows **No records**. Its older records stay in Nocturne.

These statuses are for a connection that sends records.

| Status | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| Active | The connection sent a record in the last 15 minutes. |
| Stopped | No record arrived in the last 15 minutes, and the connection sends glucose or device status all the time. It is possible that it stopped. |
| Quiet | No record arrived in the last 15 minutes, and the connection sends only records that come from time to time, such as treatments. This is normal. |

Other statuses:

- **Waiting for first use**: an API token or app that no one has used yet.
- **Error**: a connector that Nocturne fetches from reported an error.
- **Imported**: records that came from a file. Nocturne does not fetch more.
- **Off**: a connector that is turned off.
- **Revoked**: you removed the access of the app or token.

For a connection that only reads data, **Active** means that it read data in the last 24 hours.
For a connector, the status is the state of its last sync.

## Delete the data of a stream

You can delete the records of one label. Nocturne deletes all the records with that label, not
only the records of the last 30 days. A label with no record in the last 30 days is not listed.
Its records stay in Nocturne.

<Callout type="warning" title="You cannot undo a delete">

  Nocturne never imports a deleted record again, even if the source sends it again. To allow
  that, select **Allow re-import** before you delete. Then Nocturne imports the records that the
  source sends again, including the records that you deleted.

</Callout>

